.Dd July 27, 2025
.Dt CIPHERLOCK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cipherlock
.Nd AES-256-GCM file encryption with Argon2id key derivation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar flags
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Go library and CLI tool for encrypting files and directories using
AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption with Argon2id memory-hard key derivation.
It supports password-based and X25519 asymmetric encryption, streaming for
arbitrarily large files, multi-recipient encryption, and optional zstd
compression.
.Pp
All cryptographic operations are performed in memory; no intermediate
plaintext is written to disk unless explicitly requested.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm encrypt
Encrypt a file, directory, or stdin stream.
.Pp
If
.Ar path
is a regular file, it is encrypted with AES-256-GCM.
If
.Ar path
is a directory, it is archived (tar + gzip) before encryption.
If
.Ar path
is
.Sq - ,
read from stdin and write encrypted output to stdout.
.It Cm decrypt
Decrypt a file or stdin stream.
Supports all format versions (v0x02 through v0x08).
.It Cm rotor
Re-encrypt a file with a new password without decrypting to disk.
The plaintext streams through memory.
.El
.Ss Themed
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm dial
Generate an X25519 key pair for asymmetric encryption.
The private key can be passphrase-protected with Argon2id + AES-256-GCM.
.It Cm tumbler
Display metadata about an encrypted file without decrypting it.
Shows format version, KDF parameters, and (when available) the encrypted
or cleartext filename and expiration time.
.It Cm click
Verify that a password is correct for an encrypted file without
writing any output. Exits with status 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.It Cm bombe
Verify the embedded SHA-256 checksum of an encrypted file's plaintext
without writing any output.
.It Cm gate
Time-gated encryption: encrypt a file with an expiration time.
After the expiration, decryption fails.
.El
.Ss Key Management
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm config
Manage configuration profiles for Argon2id parameters.
Subcommands:
.Cm set-profile ,
.Cm list-profiles ,
.Cm show-profile ,
.Cm remove-profile .
.It Cm show-profile
Display a saved configuration profile.
.El
.Ss Utility
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm bench
Benchmark Argon2id KDF performance and recommend optimal parameters
for the current hardware.
.Pp
Runs 12 benchmarks (32-256 MB memory at time=1, 2, 3) and selects
the strongest parameters that complete within the target duration.
The recommendation can be saved to a config profile with
.Fl -save .
.It Cm shred
Securely delete files by overwriting with one pass of
cryptographically random data followed by one pass of zeros.
.It Cm completion
Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell.
.It Cm version
Print version information.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Global Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -in-place
Overwrite the source file with the encrypted/decrypted output.
The original is preserved as a
.Pa .cipherlock-bak
backup until the operation succeeds.
.It Fl -keep
When used with
.Fl -in-place ,
keep the original source file after successful encryption or decryption.
.It Fl -backup
When used with
.Fl -in-place ,
rename the original to
.Pa .bak
before writing.
.It Fl -dry-run
Validate arguments and print what would be done without writing any output.
.It Fl -recursive
Recursively process files in subdirectories (batch mode).
.It Fl -include Ar glob
Only process files matching the glob pattern (batch mode).
.It Fl -exclude Ar glob
Skip files matching the glob pattern (batch mode).
.It Fl -quiet
Suppress progress bars and KDF spinners; show compact status per file.
.It Fl -color1 .. Fl -color6
Set the color theme for output. Values 1-6 select predefined palettes.
.El
.Ss Encrypt Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -output Ar path , Fl o Ar path
Write output to the specified path.
.It Fl -out-dir Ar dir
Write all outputs to the specified directory (batch mode).
.It Fl -gen-password
Generate a cryptographically random 64-character hex password
and print it to stderr.
.It Fl -armor
Encode the encrypted output in base64 ASCII-armor format for
sharing via text or email.
.It Fl -compress
Compress plaintext with zstd before encryption.
Supported in v0x06+ formats. Auto-detected on decrypt.
.It Fl -checksum
Embed a SHA-256 checksum of the plaintext. Verified on decrypt.
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the password from a file instead of prompting interactively.
.It Fl -keychain
Read the password from the system keychain.
.It Fl -password-env Ar var
Read the password from the specified environment variable.
.It Fl -password-fd Ar n
Read the password from the specified file descriptor number
(e.g., 0 for stdin pipe).
.It Fl -password-stdin
Read the password from stdin interactively.
.It Fl -recipient Ar pwd
Add an additional recipient password (multi-recipient mode).
Can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl -recipient-pubkey Ar path
Encrypt to the specified X25519 public key (asymmetric mode).
Can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl -identity Ar path
Use the specified identity private key for asymmetric decryption.
Accepts cipherlock identity files and Ed25519 SSH private keys.
.It Fl -profile Ar name
Use a saved configuration profile for KDF parameters.
.It Fl -time Ar n
Argon2id time parameter (overrides profile).
.It Fl -memory Ar kb
Argon2id memory in KiB (overrides profile).
.It Fl -threads Ar n
Argon2id parallelism (overrides profile).
.It Fl -force
Overwrite existing output file without prompting.
.It Fl -jobs Ar n
Encrypt or decrypt multiple files concurrently using n workers.
.El
.Ss Decrypt Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -output Ar path , Fl o Ar path
Write decrypted output to the specified path.
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the password from a file.
.It Fl -password-env Ar var
Read the password from an environment variable.
.It Fl -password-fd Ar n
Read the password from a file descriptor.
.It Fl -password-stdin
Read the password from stdin.
.It Fl -ssh-privkey Ar path
Use the specified Ed25519 SSH private key as the decryption identity.
.It Fl -passphrase-file Ar path
Read the identity key passphrase from the specified file.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite existing output file without prompting.
.El
.Ss Gate Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -expires-in Ar duration
Set the expiration time for time-gated encryption.
Format is a Go duration string (e.g.,
.Sq 24h ,
.Sq 168h ,
.Sq 30m ).
.It Fl -compress
Compress plaintext with zstd before encryption.
.It Fl -checksum
Enable integrity checksum.
.It Fl -gen-password
Generate a random password.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite existing output file without prompting.
.El
.Ss Rotor (Re-key) Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -output Ar path , Fl o Ar path
Write re-keyed output to the specified path.
.It Fl -new-key-file Ar path
Read the new password from a file.
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the current password from a file.
.It Fl -new-password-env Ar var
Read the new password from an environment variable.
.It Fl -new-password-fd Ar n
Read the new password from a file descriptor.
.It Fl -new-password-stdin
Read the new password from stdin.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite existing output file without prompting.
.El
.Ss Shred Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -force
Skip confirmation prompts.
.El
.Ss Bench Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -target Ar duration
Target KDF duration (default: 1s).
Format is a Go duration string (e.g.,
.Sq 1s ,
.Sq 3s ,
.Sq 500ms ).
.It Fl -save Ar name
Save the recommended profile under the given name.
The profile can then be used with
.Fl -profile Ar name
on encrypt commands.
.El
.Sh FORMAT REFERENCE
Encrypted files begin with the 4-byte magic prefix
.Sq CV2\e0
followed by a version byte:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It v0x02
Legacy single-recipient format (non-streaming)
.It v0x03
Added optional SHA-256 checksum (non-streaming)
.It v0x04
Multi-recipient password-based (non-streaming, buffers in memory)
.It v0x05
Streaming format (no upper size limit, no metadata)
.It v0x06
Streaming format with encrypted metadata (filename, size, modtime)
.It v0x07
Streaming multi-recipient format
.It v0x08
Asymmetric X25519 format (ephemeral ECDH + HKDF + AES-256-GCM)
.El
.Pp
When compression is enabled, the
.Fl -compress
flag sets the
.Sq flagCompressed
bit in the format header. Decryption auto-detects this bit and
decompresses transparently.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
General error (wrong password, corrupted data, I/O error, etc.).
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CIPHERLOCK_CONFIG
Path to the configuration directory.
Defaults to
.Pa ~/.config/cipherlock .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/cipherlock/profiles.json
Saved configuration profiles.
.It Pa <file>.cipherlock-bak
Backup created during
.Fl -in-place
operations.
.It Pa <file>.cipherlock
Default output extension for directory encryption and gate encryption.
.It Pa <file>.encrypted
Default output extension for file encryption.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Basic Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt document.pdf
.Pp
Encrypts
.Pa document.pdf
to
.Pa document.pdf.encrypted .
.Ss Decryption
.Dl $ cipherlock decrypt document.pdf.encrypted
.Pp
Restores
.Pa document.pdf .
.Ss In-Place Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --in-place document.pdf
.Pp
Encrypts the file and replaces the original. If the operation is
interrupted, the original is preserved as
.Pa document.pdf.cipherlock-bak .
.Ss Encryption with Compression
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --compress --checksum server.log
.Pp
Compresses the plaintext with zstd, encrypts it, and embeds a
SHA-256 checksum. On decryption, compression and checksums are
handled automatically.
.Ss Multi-Recipient Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --recipient-password "alice" --recipient-password "bob" report.pdf
.Pp
Encrypts the file so that either Alice or Bob can decrypt it with
their respective password.
.Ss Asymmetric Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --recipient-pubkey alice.pub secret.txt
.Pp
Encrypts to Alice's X25519 public key. Alice decrypts with her
identity private key.
.Ss Time-Gated Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock gate encrypt --expires-in 168h contract.pdf
.Pp
Encrypts the file so it can only be decrypted within 7 days.
.Ss Pipe Mode
.Dl $ cat document.pdf | cipherlock encrypt --compress > document.enc
.Dl $ cat document.enc | cipherlock decrypt > document.pdf
.Ss Batch Encryption
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --recursive --include '*.txt' ./docs/
.Ss Re-key a File
.Dl $ cipherlock rotor secret.encrypted
.Pp
Decrypts and re-encrypts with a new password.
.Ss Generate a Key Pair
.Dl $ cipherlock dial -o ./mykeys
.Pp
Creates
.Pa mykeys/cipherlock.identity
and
.Pa mykeys/cipherlock.pub .
.Ss Check Password
.Dl $ cipherlock click secret.encrypted
.Ss Benchmark KDF Parameters
.Dl $ cipherlock bench
.Pp
Benchmarks 12 Argon2id combinations (32-256 MB memory, time=1-3) and
recommends the strongest parameters under 1 second.
.Dl $ cipherlock bench --target 3s
.Pp
Uses a 3-second target instead of the default 1 second.
.Dl $ cipherlock bench --save fast
.Pp
Saves the recommended profile to
.Pa ~/.config/cipherlock/profiles.json
as
.Sq fast .
Use it with:
.Dl $ cipherlock encrypt --profile fast document.pdf
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr age 1 ,
.Xr gpg 1
.Pp
Full documentation and source code:
.Pa https://github.com/valonmulolli/cipherlock
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Valon Mulolli Aq valon.mulolli@outlook.com
.Sh CAVEATS
As noted in
.Pa SECURITY.md ,
compression may leak information about the plaintext when an attacker
controls part of the input (CRIME/BREACH class attacks). Do not use
.Fl -compress
when encrypting data that includes attacker-controlled content.
.Pp
On SSDs with wear-leveling, the
.Cm shred
command cannot guarantee that all copies of the data are overwritten.
Full-disk encryption is recommended for SSD environments.
.Pp
The Argon2id KDF is intentionally slow (default ~2-10 seconds per key).
Use
.Cm config set-profile
to tune parameters for your hardware.
